## UI Craft: product showcase header and bento features

Stack: vanilla HTML/CSS with a few lines of JS · Theme: light + dark · States: default, hover, `:focus-visible`, active

**Assumption:** you said this is a prototype, so I skipped the foundation question and used the default neutral tokens. These are the `design-system` names, so you can later delete the `:root` blocks and link `design/tokens.css`. There is no product copy, so every name and line is a labelled placeholder. I made up no metrics, logos or testimonials.

### Tokens and architecture

- **Surfaces and text:** `--color-surface-default`, `-raised` and `-subtle`, `--color-text-default` and `-muted`, `--color-border-default` and `-strong`, `--color-action-primary-bg` and `-text`, `--color-border-focus`.
- **Glass:** `--glass-bg` and `--glass-blur`. The navbar has an opaque fallback and switches to frosted glass only under `@supports (backdrop-filter)`, so text stays legible over any content.
- **Shape, effects and layering:** `--r-xs` to `--r-xl`, `--glow`, `--btn-gloss`, and `--z-base`, `--z-sticky`, `--z-dropdown`, `--z-command`, `--z-modal`, `--z-toast`.
- **Theme switching:** the OS preference applies by default. The toggle sets `data-theme` and remembers it. If storage is blocked, the page still works.
- **Layout:** the container is 1120px max. The bento is a 6-column grid that collapses to 2 columns at 900px and 1 column at 640px. The 4px spacing grid is kept.
- **Primary action:** only the hero "Get started" button is filled. The nav and secondary actions are ghost or text.

